config, depgraph and others: small memos and local trims (remainder of the tested patch)

Smaller savings in the per-package config work: getUseMask() and
getUseForce() reuse the stacked result for equal token lists, the
ACCEPT_LICENSE stack of getMissingLicenses() is remembered per token
tuple (not when "*" makes it depend on the package), config._getitem()
finds a missing key without raising KeyError once per dict, and setcpv()
builds the RESTRICT/PROPERTIES USE set once instead of twice.

The cache of _flatten_atoms() (use_reduce of a package's dependency
strings for a USE set) moves from the per-attempt state to _frozen_config,
so that backtracking attempts share it.

_add_pkg() remembers per (package, enabled USE) whether REQUIRED_USE is
satisfied, for all backtracking attempts.

Leftovers, each a local rewrite of a hot statement: Package gets a
__bool__ that needs no Python frame (truth was taken from __len__, always
4); the metadata wrapper constructor copies the slots in a direct loop;
digraph.add() looks each node up once; dep_expand() tests the category
without splitting the cp; _pkg_use_enabled() returns at once when no USE
change is recorded; dep_check() and dep_zapdeps() test the noise level
before formatting debug messages; one line in _copy_dep_lists is
re-wrapped (no code change) so that the series ends byte-identical to the
tested tree.

On top of patches 0001-0024, resolve seconds before -> after
(median of the runs, at least 2 per figure):
  start 20.4 -> 19.6, holds 11.5 -> 10.7, masks 23.3 -> 22.1,
  py313 13.0 -> 12.2, bdeps 16.1 -> 15.1, policykit 11.7 -> 10.8
  sum of six 95.9 -> 90.5 (-5.5 s, -1.2 % of the stock sum 447.5)
Patches 0001-0025 together: 447.5 -> 90.5 s (-80 %); 447.5 is the
stock sum of the ladder run of 2026-11-20, stock was not run again here.

Merged: the config trims (4.5 s as a step of the second order, chain-
prelim2) with the two memos and the local trims (2.8 s there); none of them
is clearly above the noise alone. With this patch the tree is byte-identical
to the tested Python tree (the s10 arm, measured in the same passes, is the
same tree: 90.0 s).

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-17..20;
isolated from the full patch and measured on 2026-11-20..21. Not a human-written
change. Base: Portage 3.0.83. Test: `emerge -p -uND @world` on six states of
one system image, one resolve at a time; every run gave the same merge list
in the same order, the same number of backtracking attempts and the same
package count as unpatched 3.0.83.
